        "title": "Infrastructure Resilience: Frameworks, Metrics, and Investment",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Resilience is the capacity of infrastructure to absorb disruption, adapt to changed\nconditions, and recover to full function. It is distinct from reliability (expected\nperformance) and security (resistance to threat). A highly reliable system designed for\nnormal conditions can be completely non-resilient to unexpected events."
    },
