        "root_concepts": "[resilience]",
        "section": "infrastructure-systems",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Infrastructure Resilience: Frameworks, Metrics, and Investment",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "DISRUPTION EVENT\n                           |\n   System         100%     |\n   Functionality      -----+\n   (%)            |        |\n               80 +    ....+.........\n                  |   .    |         ...........\n               60 +  .     |                   ......\n                  | .      |                         .........\n               40 +.       |  LOSS OF FUNCTIONALITY       .....\n                  |        |  (RESILIENCE TRIANGLE)            ..\n               20 +        |                                     ..\n                  |        |                                       ...\n                0 +        |                                          .\n                           t0 (event)                                   t1 (full recovery)\n                                 TIME"
    },
    {
      "id": "03-RESILIENCE.md#012",
      "path": [
        "03-RESILIENCE.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:infrastructure-systems:03-resilience, git-history:infrastructure-systems:03-resilience]",
        "canonical_path": "infrastructure-systems/03-RESILIENCE.md",
        "concepts": "[resilience]",
        "current_path": "infrastructure-systems/03-RESILIENCE.md",
        "id": "maxim:infrastructure-systems:resilience",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "infrastructure-systems",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[resilience]",
        "section": "infrastructure-systems",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Infrastructure Resilience: Frameworks, Metrics, and Investment",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "FOUR DIMENSIONS (Bruneau):\n  ROBUSTNESS:     Ability to withstand disruption (height of trough = 1 - robustness)\n  REDUNDANCY:     Substitute resources exist during disruption (less deep trough)\n  RESOURCEFULNESS: Capacity to mobilize resources in response (recovery slope)\n  RAPIDITY:       Speed of recovery (time to full function = t1 - t0)"
    },
    {
      "id": "03-RESILIENCE.md#013",
      "path": [
        "03-RESILIENCE.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:infrastructure-systems:03-resilience, git-history:infrastructure-systems:03-resilience]",
        "canonical_path": "infrastructure-systems/03-RESILIENCE.md",
